    "done_when": "A report at ~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s21-red-ids-root-cause.md, with a JSON twin beside it, covers the 17 ids that the the-suite-is-green-at-head section 2 comment of 2026-09-29 assigns to S21: 16 in tests/test_crew.py and test_canonical_dump_equals_read_state[full] in tests/test_schema.py. For each id it records four things. (a) Whether it fails at the dispatch base, from a per-id pytest run naming the node id. The log is headed with revision, tree and command, and ends EXIT=. (b) The failing assertion or exception, quoted from that log. (c) The root cause, named at a file and line in the base tree, with the commit that introduced it where git log -S or blame finds one. (d) A class: product defect, stale test expectation, or environment-dependent. The report groups the ids by shared cause and gives each group its proposed repair write paths. It flags any group whose repair would touch tests/test_crew.py, because s22 holds a concurrent fix there. An id that passes at the base is reported as passing, with its log; it is not dropped. No repository file changes; runs go under the run directory with a basetemp outside any git repository.",
